The proposed Contributor Admin role must not be a synonym for super_admin, and it must not inherit finance, withdrawal, treasury, payout, project activation, role-management or Testnet privileges.
Recommended implementation sequence
Freeze the role contract: define exactly which Contributor actions Contributor Admin may perform; keep identity verification and role approval as separate permissions.
Resolve account binding: make the nomination target an existing Contributor record and verified Pi UID; require the candidate's authenticated Supabase Auth identity as well, with both identities bound by the same one-time nomination.
Review the legacy admin_invitation_links design: it has role/scope/token fields but no observed writer RPC and no dedicated binding to a nominated Contributor. Reuse it only if a documented minimal migration can safely add the missing binding and constraints; otherwise propose a separate, clearly named invitation/nomination model. Do not mutate Mainnet during the design phase.
Prepare a review-only database migration and RPC contract: add contributor_admin only after enumerating dependencies on the enum; implement issue, inspect/list, accept/verify, approve/grant, revoke and audit actions with server-side allowlists and transactional one-time token consumption. Preserve least privilege and avoid direct DML grants.
Prepare the camera capture and evidence-retention design: explicit consent/purpose; permission-denied and cancelled states; active camera stream only; size/type validation; private storage; short-lived access URLs; limited reviewer access; retention/deletion schedule. Use liveness verification or manual review if the assurance level requires it; do not treat an ordinary selfie as identity proof.
Test in a non-production environment: valid and mismatched Pi/Auth identities, expired/replayed/revoked invitation, missing AAL2, inactive admin, role/scope tampering, direct table writes, RLS/RPC denial, camera permission denial, gallery bypass attempts, self-review, revocation taking effect immediately, and Mainnet/Testnet isolation.
Obtain explicit approval before any deployment or Mainnet migration. No payments or payouts should be enabled as part of this feature.
Important acceptance tests
A Contributor Admin cannot call role-grant, financial, withdrawal, treasury, project-activation or payout RPCs, even by directly invoking an endpoint.
An invitation cannot be accepted by a different Pi UID, a different bound Supabase Auth identity, an unverified session, or a session without required AAL2.
Token consumption is atomic and one-time; expired/revoked/replayed tokens fail closed.
Revocation removes effective access at the next server authorization check; cached frontend state cannot preserve authority.
Selfie data is never public, never included in ordinary logs, and cannot be read by Contributors or unrelated admins.
The Mainnet admin record remains authoritative; Testnet data cannot grant a Mainnet role.
